invariant: INV-38
file: srv_out.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh srv_out
reason: srv_frag_bytes fills SRV_FRAG_MAX bytes before it flushes and
  ignores srv_out_limit, so a Certificate record carries more plaintext
  than the client's record_size_limit allows. The srv_out proof asserts
  that every sealed piece is at most srv_out_limit bytes, and fails on
  this edit.

--- old
    size_t limit = srv_out_limit(f->h->t);
--- new
    size_t limit = sizeof f->buf;
